# Privacy & Security

Call recordings and transcripts are personal data. Treat them as sensitive.

- Never log transcript text, audio content, participant names, or other PII.
  Log opaque identifiers (call IDs) instead.
- Secrets come from environment variables only. Never hardcode credentials in
  source, tests, docs, or docker-compose beyond throwaway local defaults.
- Fields holding credentials (e.g. `database_url`) use Pydantic `SecretStr` so
  they cannot leak via repr/str/logging.
- `.env` is git-ignored and must stay that way; only `.env.example` (with
  placeholder values) is committed.
- Test fixtures must use synthetic data, never real call recordings or real
  customer information.
- Stored audio, transcripts, and evaluation results must be encrypted at rest.
- Access to audio, transcripts, and evaluations is governed by role-based
  access control.
- Every evaluation must be traceable: rubric version, prompt/model
  configuration, justification, and transcript evidence.
- Access to sensitive data (audio, transcripts, evaluations) must be
  audit-logged.
